[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=UDP Broadcast and Receive v1.3\\\\Sends UDP broadcast packets containing||1
  Cmn2=MAC, UID, and Data to 255.255.255.255,\\and receives incoming UDP||1
  Cmn3=packets on the same port. Own broadcasts are always\\ignored (OS||1
  Cmn4=loopback). Uses a latched Enable input to open and close the socket.
  Cmn5=\\\\Wire format (no spaces): MAC,UID,Data\\Example: 00:00:00:00:
  Cmn6=00:00,123456789,[Type]value\\Maximum datagram 306 bytes (17 + 1||1
  Cmn7=+ 32 + 1 + 255).\\\\\\Signal Descriptions:\\\\  DIGITAL_INPUT Enable\\
  Cmn8=||4Latched. High opens the UDP socket on UDP_Port for broadcast||1
  Cmn9=send and receive.\\    Low closes the socket.\\\\  DIGITAL_INPUT||1
  Cmn10=Retrigger\\    Pulse to re-send the current MAC, UID, and Data even||1
  Cmn11=if Data has not changed\\    (sends even when Data is empty). Ignored||1
  Cmn12=unless the socket is open.\\\\  STRING_INPUT Mac[17]\\    MAC address||1
  Cmn13=included in the broadcast packet. Formatted to colon separators\\
  Cmn14=||4when the string is 12 hex digits (no separator) or 17 bytes||1
  Cmn15=with : or - separators.\\\\  STRING_INPUT UID[32]\\    Unique identifier||1
  Cmn16=included in the broadcast packet. Alphanumeric, up to 32 bytes.\\
  Cmn17=\\  STRING_INPUT Data[255]\\    Data to broadcast. A change on this||1
  Cmn18=input sends a packet when Data is non-empty.\\\\  DIGITAL_OUTPUT||1
  Cmn19=Enable_FB\\    High while the UDP socket is open. Low if Enable||1
  Cmn20=is low or SocketUDP_Enable failed.\\\\  STRING_OUTPUT Received_IP\\
  Cmn21=||4IP address of the sender of the last accepted packet.\\\\  STRING_OUTPUT||1
  Cmn22=Received_MAC\\    MAC parsed from the last accepted packet (colon-
  Cmn23=separated when recognized).\\\\  STRING_OUTPUT Received_UID\\||3
  Cmn24=||1UID parsed from the last accepted packet.\\\\  STRING_OUTPUT Received_Data\\
  Cmn25=||4Data parsed from the last accepted packet, or the entire payload||1
  Cmn26=when the\\    packet is not a structured MAC,UID,Data datagram.\\
  Cmn27=\\\\  INTEGER_PARAMETER UDP_Port\\    UDP port for broadcasting||1
  Cmn28=and receiving (1024-65535, default 50001).\\\\  INTEGER_PARAMETER||1
  Cmn29=Enforce_Format\\    0d = No enforcement (default): clear outputs,||1
  Cmn30=then fill only fields that\\         matched. If nothing looks like||1
  Cmn31=a MAC or UID, Received_IP and\\         Received_Data get the sender||1
  Cmn32=IP and the entire payload.\\    1d = Enforce MAC,UID,Data: only||1
  Cmn33=a valid full packet updates the outputs;\\         any other datagram||1
  Cmn34=is ignored (last good values kept).\\\\\\Receive parsing (No enforcement):
  Cmn35=\\  1. Clear all four received outputs.\\  2. Write Received_IP||1
  Cmn36=when the sender IP is known.\\  3. If the payload is MAC,UID,Data||1
  Cmn37=(two commas, field 1 is a MAC, field 2 is a UID),\\     fill MAC,||1
  Cmn38=UID, and Data (Data may be empty).\\  4. If field 1 is a MAC but||1
  Cmn39=field 2 is not a UID, fill MAC and treat the remainder\\     as||1
  Cmn40=Data.\\  5. If no field looks like a MAC or UID, Received_Data is||1
  Cmn41=the entire payload.\\\\Own packets (MAC + UID match this module,||1
  Cmn42=or the payload equals what this module\\would send) never update||1
  Cmn43=the received outputs.\\\\MAC shape: 12 hex digits, or 17 bytes as||1
  Cmn44=six hex pairs separated by : or -.\\UID shape: 1-32 bytes, letters,||1
  Cmn45=digits, hyphen, or underscore.\\\\ _____\\ | ~~~ |\\ | O-O |\\ |/\/\/\/\|\\
  Cmn46=||1|\/\/\/\/|\\ ---------\\\\-- VERSION HISTORY --\\v1.3  2026-09-
  Cmn47=09\\- Latched Enable / Enable_FB; SocketUDP_Disable on Enable low\\
  Cmn48=- Retrigger pulse to re-send current packet\\- Enforce_Format parameter||1
  Cmn49=(default: no enforcement)\\- Receive: clear then fill; unstructured||1
  Cmn50=payloads -> IP + Data only\\- Always ignore own broadcasts\\- Fix||1
  Cmn51=outgoing packet size (306), FormatMAC 12-byte length check,\\  SocketGetSenderIPA
  Cmn52=ddress error test, Main() startup Enable\\\\v1.2\\- Broadcast MAC,UID,Data||1
  Cmn53=and parse incoming UDP on a configurable port\\
[END]
